<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Injuid dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1335 CE – 1357 CE (approx.) · capital Shiraz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived dynasty that ruled Shiraz after the fall of the Ilkhans, whose ruler Abu Ishaq was the generous patron of the young Hafez.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharaf-al-din-mahmud-shah">Sharaf al-Din Mahmud Shah</a> was appointed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> to manage the crown estates (inju) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-said-bahadur-khan">Abu Sa'id</a> died in 1335, his family made itself master of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> and the province.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Injuids ruled a wealthy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> where poetry and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufism</a> flourished. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-ishaq-inju">Abu Ishaq Inju</a>, who took power around 1343, was a cultivated and lavish ruler; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> visited his court, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a> and the satirist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubayd-zakani">Ubayd Zakani</a> praised him. He was also reckless, and his rivalry with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/muzaffarid-dynasty">Muzaffarids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> drained his treasury.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/muzaffarid-dynasty">Muzaffarid dynasty</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> in 1353. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-ishaq-inju">Abu Ishaq</a> fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, was captured and executed in 1357, ending the dynasty.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1335 CE – 1357 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.27%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1335 CE – 1357 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shiraz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mahmud Shah Inju, Abu Ishaq Inju</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Injuids, Inju dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1346&amp;focus=injuid-dynasty" aria-label="Injuid dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6047 1096 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Injuid dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6367 1352L6134 1224M6367 1352L6367 1352"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0M6367 1352h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6367 1352h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6367 1352h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Shiraz. <a href="/atlas?year=1346&amp;focus=injuid-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
